    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2100" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἶα</span></b>  (A), ἡ, 
			Ep.
		 form used for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γαῖα</span> metri
		gr., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυσίζοος αἶα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.243
				</span></i>
			, etc., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Scol.</u>
				12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.580
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tab.Defix.</u>
				7
			</span></i>; also in Trag., chiefly in lyr., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				59
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				95
			</span></i>, also in trim., <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				51
			</span></i>: never in pl. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἶα, ἡ</span>,
			orig. name of Colchis, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				914
			</span></i>: also part of Thessaly, ib.<i><span class="en">
				915
			</span></i>.</div>
